WEBVTT

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.958
"I give permission to make
'Excel Saga' Japanimation-ish."

00:00:29.958 --> 00:00:31.458
You suck!

00:00:31.958 --> 00:00:33.167
"Excel Saga"

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:33.917
"Excel Saga"
"Koshi Rikdo"

00:00:44.625 --> 00:00:48.500
<i>That isn't love</i>

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:52.333
<i>Love isn't that</i>

00:00:52.333 --> 00:01:00.250
<i>I am in love, but I am not loved</i>

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:04.125
<i>Definitely isn't love</i>

00:01:04.125 --> 00:01:08.125
<i>Derriere isn't love</i>

00:01:08.125 --> 00:01:15.875
<i>I want to be loved,</i>
<i>but I never seek it out</i>

00:01:16.833 --> 00:01:20.708
<i>I offer myself and throw my life away</i>

00:01:20.708 --> 00:01:24.708
<i>Looking neither left nor right,</i>
<i>I will just earnestly</i>

00:01:24.708 --> 00:01:28.667
<i>Cheat, wheedle, interfere</i>

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:31.875
<i>And trample down and</i>
<i>kick strangers</i>

00:01:31.875 --> 00:01:34.125
<i>And we get the hell out!</i>
<i>(And we get the hell out!)</i>

00:01:34.125 --> 00:01:36.042
<i>And we get the hell out!</i>
<i>(And we get the hell out!)</i>

00:01:36.042 --> 00:01:37.750
<i>And we get the hell out!</i>
<i>(And we get the hell out!)</i>

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:39.792
<i>And we get the hell out!</i>

00:01:39.792 --> 00:01:44.542
<i>Even if I slip on a banana peel</i>

00:01:44.542 --> 00:01:47.750
<i>It is all for his sake anyway</i>

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:52.292
<i>If anything, that is probably</i>

00:01:52.292 --> 00:02:00.125
<i>A kind of loyalty called love</i>

00:02:06.917 --> 00:02:09.083
Hail, Ilpalazzo!

00:02:09.083 --> 00:02:09.667
Zzo.

00:02:09.667 --> 00:02:13.458
Good morning, Excel and Hyatt.

00:02:14.292 --> 00:02:17.083
Our ACROSS's
city conquest operation

00:02:17.083 --> 00:02:19.917
is getting to a very nice phase.

00:02:19.917 --> 00:02:23.000
Of course, there is still
a long road ahead to success,

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:24.625
but I think it can be said

00:02:24.625 --> 00:02:27.417
that it is hardly too late
to think about the next step.

00:02:27.417 --> 00:02:29.083
Lord Ilpalazzo,

00:02:29.083 --> 00:02:32.792
I feel as though you are
speaking differently than normal.

00:02:32.792 --> 00:02:35.167
Oh, sorry.

00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:39.125
In other words,
I would like you to keep in mind

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:42.417
the next step to
the conquest of this city.

00:02:42.417 --> 00:02:43.917
Oh, I see!

00:02:43.917 --> 00:02:46.417
You always have your
sights set squarely on the future.

00:02:46.417 --> 00:02:48.792
I, Excel, have deep respect
for that position, Lord Ilpalazzo!

00:02:48.792 --> 00:02:49.792
Thank you.

00:02:49.792 --> 00:02:52.708
So what should we do, specifically?

00:02:52.708 --> 00:02:55.625
I wish to order you two to
go on an overseas business trip.

00:02:55.625 --> 00:02:57.000
Overseas?!

00:02:59.458 --> 00:03:03.000
In order to smoothly
propel forward our ideal,

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.792
I want you to get an accurate grasp

00:03:04.792 --> 00:03:06.792
of the conditions of
each country, starting now.

00:03:06.792 --> 00:03:08.125
I understand!

00:03:08.125 --> 00:03:10.708
I, Excel, will go anywhere,
if it is Lord Ilpalazzo's command!

00:03:10.708 --> 00:03:12.167
Be it the ends of the Earth!

00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:13.750
Or be it the bottom of the ocean!

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:16.792
Or be it a country that is both
dangerous to get in and out of!

00:03:16.792 --> 00:03:20.167
Senior, do you have
a passport and such?

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:22.375
No! But I'll get by
with my guts somehow!

00:03:22.375 --> 00:03:25.000
I have already prepared
a means of entering the country.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.542
Oh, that, right?

00:03:26.542 --> 00:03:28.042
Yes, this.

00:03:28.042 --> 00:03:30.167
I'll be going now!

00:03:30.167 --> 00:03:33.167
Wow, it really is long,
it's awesome, Lord Ilpalazzo!

00:03:33.167 --> 00:03:35.833
Saving travel costs, no need for
customs! A dream means of travel!

00:03:35.833 --> 00:03:37.875
Such a handsome idea that
gives cost performance top priority!

00:03:37.875 --> 00:03:40.917
Right now, I'm beyond doubts
and more prone to feeling impressed!

00:03:40.917 --> 00:03:43.333
I continue to fall and
where am I going to end up?!

00:03:43.333 --> 00:03:46.000
I remember such things
as forgetting to ask about that,

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.042
but even as I say this...

00:03:47.042 --> 00:03:49.167
I've already reached the mantle?!

00:03:52.833 --> 00:03:55.833
Following this is the
mysterious underground space!

00:03:55.833 --> 00:03:58.542
Kids, don't you try this at home!

00:04:19.208 --> 00:04:21.875
I have arrived!

00:04:21.875 --> 00:04:22.750
Oh!

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:23.833
What?!

00:04:23.833 --> 00:04:25.208
Jesus!

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:31.667
All right! Excel is here!

00:04:40.833 --> 00:04:43.333
The very picture of a slum town!

00:04:44.333 --> 00:04:46.417
Then, that means this is...

00:04:47.417 --> 00:04:49.000
America!

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.167
Entered country successfully!

00:04:50.167 --> 00:04:52.083
Now that I know, time to check out

00:04:52.083 --> 00:04:54.917
the situation of America,
the great, ill country!

00:04:54.917 --> 00:04:56.417
Oh?

00:04:58.875 --> 00:05:02.292
What might this unfriendly feeling be?

00:05:02.292 --> 00:05:05.583
It seems that everyone is distrustful of us.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:08.458
Wow! When in the world?!

00:05:08.458 --> 00:05:10.917
Senior, why not begin with
a self-introduction

00:05:10.917 --> 00:05:13.583
and put their worries to rest?

00:05:13.583 --> 00:05:15.417
O-Okay, okay.

00:05:15.417 --> 00:05:19.958
Hello! Merry Christmas, I'm Excel!

00:05:19.958 --> 00:05:22.167
Y-You are dog!

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:25.125
Could it just be me?

00:05:25.125 --> 00:05:28.625
I feel as though the atmosphere
has worsened even more.

00:05:28.625 --> 00:05:31.042
I just strung together all
the words I knew.

00:05:31.042 --> 00:05:33.792
Did it bother them?
Did I pick a fight with them?

00:05:33.792 --> 00:05:35.167
Shit!

00:05:35.167 --> 00:05:37.125
The US-Japan friendship
has broken down!

00:05:37.125 --> 00:05:38.792
Is the language barrier truly that great?!

00:05:38.792 --> 00:05:41.458
One minute after arriving,
and we are already in a big fix.

00:05:41.458 --> 00:05:42.417
No, no.

00:05:42.417 --> 00:05:45.625
If I speak with sincerity,
surely it'll get my meaning across.

00:05:45.625 --> 00:05:48.208
Y-Your mother is a pig!

00:05:50.792 --> 00:05:53.458
Senior, I feel as though
the gap between your sincerity

00:05:53.458 --> 00:05:55.042
and your vocabulary is too big.

00:05:55.042 --> 00:05:58.000
Oh, why are these the only
words that come to my mind?!

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.375
My regret is as big as a mountain.

00:06:01.458 --> 00:06:03.250
You're going to blame me
and beat me, aren't you?

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:05.333
Excel is in a fix and in danger!

00:06:10.167 --> 00:06:11.917
It's Puni Puni Poemy!

00:06:11.917 --> 00:06:13.333
Poemy!

00:06:14.042 --> 00:06:15.333
--There's more over here!

00:06:15.333 --> 00:06:17.000
--Poemy! Poemy!
--There's more over here!

00:06:18.458 --> 00:06:21.833
Hatchan, what is this situation...

00:06:21.833 --> 00:06:24.125
Now's your chance! Hurry!

00:06:24.125 --> 00:06:25.125
This way!

00:06:25.125 --> 00:06:26.917
What?!

00:06:26.917 --> 00:06:28.333
Hand it over!

00:06:28.333 --> 00:06:29.667
I won't let go!

00:06:32.542 --> 00:06:34.000
You okay?

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:35.667
That was close.

00:06:35.667 --> 00:06:38.458
Man, you saved us.
That escape from death was narrow.

00:06:38.458 --> 00:06:41.167
By the way, who might you be?

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:43.625
I'm Sandora. What about you?

00:06:43.625 --> 00:06:45.042
I'm Excel!

00:06:45.042 --> 00:06:46.958
My name is Hyatt.

00:06:46.958 --> 00:06:49.833
You're involved with
Japanimation, aren't you?

00:06:49.833 --> 00:06:50.542
--Japa?

00:06:50.542 --> 00:06:52.375
--I can tell by the way you're dressed.
--Japa?

00:06:52.375 --> 00:06:54.208
You're cosplayers, right?

00:06:54.208 --> 00:06:57.875
No, this is sort of like a work uniform.

00:06:57.875 --> 00:06:59.583
I have a favor to ask.

00:06:59.583 --> 00:07:02.708
Teach me about Japanimation!

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:06.167
"Poemy"

00:07:06.625 --> 00:07:08.458
Have a seat somewhere.

00:07:08.458 --> 00:07:10.292
Sorry to intrude.

00:07:16.583 --> 00:07:19.375
It is hard to believe
that this room is in New York.

00:07:19.375 --> 00:07:21.375
Are you an animator?

00:07:21.375 --> 00:07:22.875
I'm just an apprentice.

00:07:22.875 --> 00:07:26.625
Actually, I want to be a
professional soccer player,

00:07:26.625 --> 00:07:29.417
but they said kids can't join.

00:07:29.417 --> 00:07:32.042
Boss picked me up when
I didn't know what to do.

00:07:32.042 --> 00:07:34.750
So, now, I draw key animation
like the ones you saw

00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:37.292
and deliver them to Boss.

00:07:37.292 --> 00:07:38.875
I've heard the rumors.

00:07:38.875 --> 00:07:39.917
About what?

00:07:39.917 --> 00:07:43.500
Anime's turning into a movement
in Japan right now, right?

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:45.875
A hundred episodes
are broadcast every week

00:07:45.875 --> 00:07:49.417
and animators have so much
work they don't have time to sleep!

00:07:49.417 --> 00:07:52.250
In Japan, the job of the
animator is the super-occupation

00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:54.417
and they're highly
sought after, right? Right?!

00:07:54.417 --> 00:07:57.667
It seems that only a fragment of
the information has gotten across.

00:07:57.667 --> 00:07:59.125
Looks like it.

00:07:59.125 --> 00:08:01.417
I'm going to become a popular animator,

00:08:01.417 --> 00:08:03.708
make lots and lots of money,

00:08:03.708 --> 00:08:06.167
and make Mom happy.

00:08:06.167 --> 00:08:08.792
Is your mother suffering hardship?

00:08:08.792 --> 00:08:13.292
No, she lives in ecstasy
with Dad in the countryside.

00:08:13.292 --> 00:08:14.917
Then that's good!

00:08:14.917 --> 00:08:18.958
But that Dad isn't my real dad!

00:08:19.667 --> 00:08:25.250
My real dad went to work in Japan,
but he was in an accident.

00:08:26.125 --> 00:08:28.917
My current dad was a
good person in the beginning,

00:08:28.917 --> 00:08:31.708
but he's gotten into gambling now.

00:08:31.708 --> 00:08:33.500
On top of that, he always loses

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:37.625
and now he's even dipping into
Mom's postal savings!

00:08:38.625 --> 00:08:41.375
A dad without money isn't Dad!

00:08:41.375 --> 00:08:42.667
That's brutally frank.

00:08:42.667 --> 00:08:45.708
Truly the nation most
advanced in capitalism.

00:08:45.708 --> 00:08:49.333
That's why I'm going to
become a famous animator

00:08:49.333 --> 00:08:52.042
and give Mom a comfortable life.

00:08:52.042 --> 00:08:53.625
Sandora!

00:08:53.625 --> 00:08:55.125
Boss!

00:08:57.625 --> 00:09:01.083
Guarandoo! And boomerang!

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:06.917
Sandora, who are these women?

00:09:09.625 --> 00:09:10.958
Hello!

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:19.417
Sandora, two at once?
You're quite an enthusiastic boy.

00:09:19.417 --> 00:09:20.750
What are you talking about?

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:23.292
I guess you're already
getting to be that age.

00:09:23.292 --> 00:09:25.875
I know. I understand.

00:09:25.875 --> 00:09:28.375
I won't tell your mom.

00:09:28.375 --> 00:09:31.042
It seems that there
is a misunderstanding.

00:09:31.042 --> 00:09:35.250
You look quiet, but you catch
onto these things right away, Hatchan.

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:37.542
By the way, are the goods ready?

00:09:37.542 --> 00:09:39.208
Just a little more.

00:09:46.917 --> 00:09:48.417
They're well done.

00:09:48.417 --> 00:09:50.208
Thank you, Boss!

00:09:50.208 --> 00:09:51.792
With your key animation,

00:09:51.792 --> 00:09:54.125
the project will undoubtedly be a success!

00:09:54.125 --> 00:09:55.708
No, please.

00:09:55.708 --> 00:09:57.708
No need to be modest.

00:09:57.708 --> 00:09:59.667
When your drawings
become Japanimation

00:09:59.667 --> 00:10:01.792
and it goes on air all over the world,

00:10:01.792 --> 00:10:03.542
I'm sure your mom will be very happy.

00:10:03.542 --> 00:10:05.125
Yes! I'll work hard!

00:10:05.125 --> 00:10:07.542
Finish these up for me by tomorrow.

00:10:07.542 --> 00:10:10.250
Korean mail goes out first thing
in the morning day after tomorrow,

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:13.292
so we'll need the
color model guide by then.

00:10:13.292 --> 00:10:14.083
Yes, Sir.

00:10:14.083 --> 00:10:18.417
I wonder how many anime
shows actually still use cels?

00:10:18.417 --> 00:10:19.375
Uh-oh.

00:10:19.375 --> 00:10:23.333
I hear digital has been
on the rise in recent works.

00:10:23.333 --> 00:10:25.292
Like so.

00:10:25.292 --> 00:10:27.125
Uh-oh, uh-oh, uh-oh.

00:10:27.125 --> 00:10:32.125
S-Sandora, I'll be going now.
I don't want to get in your way.

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:36.250
Now, you two go home too.

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:37.875
Go home? But...

00:10:37.875 --> 00:10:38.917
Shut up!

00:10:38.917 --> 00:10:40.083
Hey!

00:10:40.083 --> 00:10:42.750
Well, I'm counting on you, Sandora.

00:10:46.167 --> 00:10:47.333
What was all that?

00:10:47.333 --> 00:10:49.875
What the hell?! That was rude!

00:10:49.875 --> 00:10:51.583
You should be more gentle.

00:10:51.583 --> 00:10:53.625
You two, don't say
such unnecessary things!

00:10:53.625 --> 00:10:56.125
Wh-What unnecessary things?!

00:10:56.125 --> 00:10:58.958
We only voiced a
simple problematic point.

00:10:58.958 --> 00:11:00.958
And that's what was unnecessary!

00:11:00.958 --> 00:11:04.083
Don't go near Sandora, got it?!

00:11:04.083 --> 00:11:06.083
Why only me?!

00:11:11.542 --> 00:11:16.250
Dick, let's trade the goods
I promised the day after tomorrow.

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:17.958
Yeah, they're great quality.

00:11:17.958 --> 00:11:20.542
They're one of a kind valuables.

00:11:25.083 --> 00:11:27.083
I smell a conspiracy.

00:11:30.125 --> 00:11:31.458
Senior!

00:11:31.458 --> 00:11:34.042
Acting independently is a problem.

00:11:34.167 --> 00:11:35.000
"Gomez"

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:36.667
Dear!

00:11:36.667 --> 00:11:39.250
That's the money Sandora earned!

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:42.500
So that I could keep on
doing nothing but goofing off!

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:46.667
Shut up! Your money is,
by definition, my money!

00:11:46.667 --> 00:11:49.667
I'll double it and let you do lots
more of nothing but goofing off,

00:11:49.667 --> 00:11:50.500
--so be quiet and hand it over!

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:52.792
--You say that, but all you ever do is lose!
--so be quiet and hand it over!

00:11:52.792 --> 00:11:54.125
Shut up!

00:11:54.125 --> 00:11:55.458
Ouch!

00:11:57.500 --> 00:12:00.000
Are you all right, Dear?

00:12:04.167 --> 00:12:06.000
I'm on fire!

00:12:09.167 --> 00:12:11.167
My old Dear!

00:12:11.167 --> 00:12:12.542
Pedro!

00:12:24.583 --> 00:12:27.167
Long time no see, Gomez.

00:12:27.167 --> 00:12:29.542
Wh-What did you come here for, Pedro?!

00:12:29.542 --> 00:12:30.792
This is revenge!

00:12:30.792 --> 00:12:34.708
You were Mr. Pe's friend,
and yet you stole everything from him!

00:12:34.708 --> 00:12:37.292
Hateful Gomez! You bastard, Gomez!

00:12:37.292 --> 00:12:38.708
Revenge?

00:12:38.708 --> 00:12:43.875
That's right. Mr. Pe has come back
to settle this once and for all with you.

00:12:43.875 --> 00:12:48.208
Yes! They were hard days
of intensive training.

00:12:52.583 --> 00:12:53.833
Yuck.

00:13:24.583 --> 00:13:34.083
Pedro! Pedro! Pedro! Pedro!

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:41.125
That was long, you idiot!

00:13:41.125 --> 00:13:44.917
Shut up! Those numerous
trials have changed me!

00:13:44.917 --> 00:13:48.917
Now is the time for you
to know my wrath, Gomez!

00:13:51.542 --> 00:13:55.458
Dear, you're so awesome.

00:13:55.458 --> 00:13:57.000
Don't twinkle, you idiot!

00:13:57.000 --> 00:14:00.583
Shut up! What's wrong with
twinkling, you nincompoop?!

00:14:00.583 --> 00:14:04.875
In any case,
you will know my wrath, Gomez!

00:14:07.167 --> 00:14:10.292
Once again, you're so awesome.

00:14:11.083 --> 00:14:14.708
Quit havin' tea and start fighting!

00:14:14.708 --> 00:14:16.208
Yes, indeed!

00:14:16.208 --> 00:14:18.792
You've acted rashly, Great Will.

00:14:18.792 --> 00:14:21.458
Right now, Pedro still
isn't ready to face Gomez.

00:14:21.458 --> 00:14:23.417
The water's seeping in! It's seeping in!

00:14:23.417 --> 00:14:24.417
It's seeping in!

00:14:24.417 --> 00:14:29.875
♪ Dangerous seeming deals ♪

00:14:29.875 --> 00:14:34.083
♪ should be done in the harbor
warehouse district at night. ♪

00:14:34.083 --> 00:14:38.667
♪ Lululu, white powder... ♪

00:14:38.667 --> 00:14:40.875
Shut up! Kill them!

00:14:52.917 --> 00:14:53.958
Dick!

00:14:53.958 --> 00:14:55.958
Corleone!

00:14:55.958 --> 00:14:58.542
It's good to be alive!

00:14:58.542 --> 00:15:00.958
Haven't seen you in a while, Corleone.

00:15:00.958 --> 00:15:02.208
You're right, Dick.

00:15:02.208 --> 00:15:04.208
Not since that matter down in Columbia.

00:15:04.208 --> 00:15:06.583
We both sure have the Devil's own luck.

00:15:06.583 --> 00:15:08.417
Meaninglessly...

00:15:09.542 --> 00:15:13.000
We have lots to catch up on,
but first, let's finish the deal.

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:15.708
Is the Puni Puni Poemy key
animation done?

00:15:15.708 --> 00:15:20.750
Of course. But before that,
I'd like to see the money.

00:15:20.750 --> 00:15:22.417
Sure thing.

00:15:27.875 --> 00:15:31.625
A million dollars, as promised.
And where are the goods?

00:15:31.625 --> 00:15:32.958
Fine.

00:15:36.583 --> 00:15:38.875
I'll take a look at it, just to be safe.

00:15:38.875 --> 00:15:42.417
Boss!

00:15:42.417 --> 00:15:45.375
Sandora, why, what are
you doing here right now?

00:15:45.375 --> 00:15:51.750
Boss, wasn't my key animation
supposed to become Japanimation?!

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:54.250
Boss, did you trick me?

00:15:57.125 --> 00:15:59.750
That's exactly what I did, Sandora.

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:02.000
The cels made from your key animation

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:04.292
will be sold as fakes on the black market.

00:16:05.083 --> 00:16:06.917
Shock!

00:16:06.917 --> 00:16:11.333
This is a lot quicker than making
expensive things like anime.

00:16:11.333 --> 00:16:13.583
Besides, there's no way art
created in America

00:16:13.583 --> 00:16:16.250
would become Japanimation!

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:21.458
Of course! One more time, shock!
Shock, shock...

00:16:21.458 --> 00:16:24.958
Then I can't become a famous animator?

00:16:24.958 --> 00:16:28.167
Maybe that was a little harsh for a kid.

00:16:28.167 --> 00:16:30.958
Corleone, regardless
of what your situation is,

00:16:30.958 --> 00:16:32.458
let's have the key animation.

00:16:32.458 --> 00:16:34.792
Sorry, my friend.

00:16:34.792 --> 00:16:35.500
--Hey.

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:36.958
--Yes, Boss.
--Hey.

00:16:36.958 --> 00:16:38.500
Now, take a look at this, Dick.

00:16:38.500 --> 00:16:40.208
Here's the promised goods.

00:16:40.208 --> 00:16:42.875
Top quality stuff,
with timing sheets included.

00:16:42.875 --> 00:16:44.958
It better be.

00:16:44.958 --> 00:16:46.958
What's the matter, my friend?

00:16:47.333 --> 00:16:48.667
Shit!

00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:52.625
Wha-What are you doing?!

00:16:52.625 --> 00:16:54.375
Never mind, just take a look.

00:16:54.375 --> 00:16:55.625
The-These are...

00:16:55.625 --> 00:16:59.208
That isn't Puni Puni Poemy!
That's Samurai Maccione!

00:16:59.208 --> 00:17:01.542
Well, wait, that's rare in itself too,

00:17:01.542 --> 00:17:03.958
but what is going on here, Corleone?!

00:17:03.958 --> 00:17:05.750
N-No, this is...

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:06.958
Sandora!

00:17:06.958 --> 00:17:10.083
When I learned
that you were tricking me,

00:17:10.083 --> 00:17:12.333
I switched the contents of the folder!

00:17:12.333 --> 00:17:14.000
What?! Who in the world...

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:18.042
Corleone, this deal is off.
I'm not paying for this.

00:17:18.042 --> 00:17:20.000
But that's a shock!

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:22.000
Since it's come to this...

00:17:25.083 --> 00:17:28.500
The deal is off. I won't go easy on you.

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:30.917
Guess I have no choice.
I can't just let you get away with that.

00:17:30.917 --> 00:17:32.042
Stop the fight!

00:17:32.042 --> 00:17:32.583
--Who's that?!

00:17:32.583 --> 00:17:34.292
--Stop those two!
--Who's that?!

00:17:36.583 --> 00:17:39.667
I'm Excel! Main character!

00:17:39.667 --> 00:17:41.333
You didn't...

00:17:41.333 --> 00:17:43.000
A cosplayer!

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:44.667
Miss Excel!

00:17:46.583 --> 00:17:47.250
--Japanimation has its own good points

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:48.250
--What the heck?
--Japanimation has its own good points

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:51.417
--She has her back to us.
--and so does America!

00:17:51.417 --> 00:17:54.083
That's what's so
wonderful about animation!

00:17:54.083 --> 00:17:55.042
However!

00:17:55.042 --> 00:17:58.375
I will not forgive those
who do not see that

00:17:58.375 --> 00:18:00.375
and only care about personal gain.

00:18:01.042 --> 00:18:04.875
For guys like you,
in the name of the moon,

00:18:04.875 --> 00:18:06.250
I shall spank you!

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:09.667
Oh, that's a Japanimation
from just a while back.

00:18:09.667 --> 00:18:11.875
Um, um...

00:18:11.875 --> 00:18:14.833
It's Sailor... right?

00:18:14.833 --> 00:18:18.375
However, that anime's already over.

00:18:18.375 --> 00:18:19.375
Shut up!

00:18:19.375 --> 00:18:22.042
I was doing good with this
stuff until just a couple years back!

00:18:22.042 --> 00:18:23.875
Never mind! Shoot her!

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:27.375
Common sense number one
in Japanimation!

00:18:27.375 --> 00:18:29.875
The bullets never hit the heroine!

00:18:29.875 --> 00:18:31.542
Number two!

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:37.042
Meaningless explosions take care
of the small fry in one fell swoop!

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:39.292
D-Damn!

00:18:39.292 --> 00:18:40.625
Number three!

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:51.167
Really extreme scenes
depend on acting skill.

00:18:51.167 --> 00:18:52.167
You bastards!

00:18:52.167 --> 00:18:55.625
And now, we'll switch to the
American animation category!

00:18:56.792 --> 00:18:58.292
Wonder!

00:19:01.792 --> 00:19:03.083
Get her!

00:19:03.083 --> 00:19:04.917
Number one!

00:19:04.917 --> 00:19:05.833
Ouch!

00:19:05.833 --> 00:19:08.750
The heroine's punch is absolutely lethal!

00:19:14.625 --> 00:19:14.708
Number two!

00:19:14.708 --> 00:19:16.625
Number two!

00:19:18.833 --> 00:19:20.708
Hatchan, please!

00:19:20.708 --> 00:19:22.042
Snip.

00:19:30.292 --> 00:19:32.333
Number three!

00:19:33.333 --> 00:19:35.458
No! No!

00:19:35.458 --> 00:19:38.167
Even defeating bad guys
is full of humor!

00:19:42.125 --> 00:19:44.625
Viva animation!

00:19:51.292 --> 00:19:54.125
Thank you, Miss Excel and Miss Hyatt.

00:19:54.125 --> 00:19:56.375
I have renewed awe for anime.

00:19:56.375 --> 00:19:58.167
Not at all. Now we're even.

00:19:58.167 --> 00:20:01.333
After all, you saved us as well.

00:20:01.333 --> 00:20:05.000
I'm going back to the countryside
to stay close to my mom.

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:08.750
When I grow up, this time,
I'll definitely become a soccer player!

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:11.625
Please say hello to your mother for us.

00:20:11.625 --> 00:20:13.333
Thank you!

00:20:16.542 --> 00:20:18.167
There we go.

00:20:18.167 --> 00:20:18.958
Bye.

00:20:18.958 --> 00:20:22.500
Please excuse us.

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:27.500
Thank you! Goodbye!

00:20:28.542 --> 00:20:29.250
"ACROSS"   "Space"   "Earth Ball"
"Excel and Hyatt"

00:20:29.250 --> 00:20:30.167
"ACROSS"   "Space"   "Earth Ball"
Hatchan,

00:20:30.167 --> 00:20:32.000
"ACROSS"   "Space"   "Earth Ball"
I sort of have the feeling

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:34.500
"ACROSS"   "Space"   "Earth Ball"
that we've seen that kid before!

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:36.500
"ACROSS"   "Space"   "Earth Ball"
Where did you see him?

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:36.875
"ACROSS"   "Space"   "Earth Ball"

00:20:36.875 --> 00:20:38.708
"ACROSS"   "Space"   "Earth Ball"
I can't remember!

00:20:50.792 --> 00:20:52.542
No!

00:21:04.500 --> 00:21:05.125
"Doable In One Week"
"English Conversation I"

00:21:05.125 --> 00:21:07.417
This is Ilpalazzo.

00:21:07.417 --> 00:21:09.708
I am coquettish.

00:21:09.708 --> 00:21:11.208
We have just returned!

00:21:11.208 --> 00:21:13.583
Hail, Ilpala...

00:21:13.583 --> 00:21:14.542
...zzo.

00:21:14.542 --> 00:21:17.042
How was the overseas business trip?

00:21:17.042 --> 00:21:19.167
It was truly a worthwhile business trip!

00:21:19.167 --> 00:21:21.583
So much so, that differences in location
and time didn't bother me at all!

00:21:21.583 --> 00:21:23.417
We purged evil and saved a person!

00:21:23.417 --> 00:21:26.458
It's another episode
of a nice ACROSS story!

00:21:26.458 --> 00:21:30.375
I see. And were you able
to grasp the situation there?

00:21:30.375 --> 00:21:32.917
I am asking if you were
able to get an accurate perception

00:21:32.917 --> 00:21:35.583
of an advanced nation's current state.

00:21:35.583 --> 00:21:37.417
Oh, well, that is...

00:21:37.417 --> 00:21:40.083
America is a slum, the stink
all in a row, bats are bang-bang,

00:21:40.083 --> 00:21:41.833
and Mafia making deals in warehouses.

00:21:41.833 --> 00:21:45.250
It was like, the American dream is
a dream beyond a dream.

00:21:45.250 --> 00:21:46.417
Right, Hatchan?

00:21:46.417 --> 00:21:50.833
I do not know. It was all
I could do to keep up with you.

00:21:50.833 --> 00:21:52.417
Go there one more time.

00:21:52.417 --> 00:21:54.250
Once more?!

00:21:54.250 --> 00:21:56.250
Oh, why just me?!

00:22:13.458 --> 00:22:15.167
Where am I?!

00:22:16.458 --> 00:22:20.792
"Episode 17: Animation USA"

00:22:20.792 --> 00:22:22.542
"Episode 17: Animation USA"
"Today's Experiment..."

00:22:22.542 --> 00:22:24.417
"Episode 17: Animation USA"
"Today's Experiment... NG"

00:22:25.833 --> 00:22:28.958
"Gettin' irritated isn't
gonna get you anywhere."

00:22:51.042 --> 00:22:59.417
<i>I knew, ever since that day</i>

00:22:59.417 --> 00:23:06.833
<i>The reason you had approached me</i>

00:23:06.833 --> 00:23:15.000
<i>Tender and soft</i>

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:23.750
<i>That my body is to your taste</i>

00:23:24.708 --> 00:23:32.500
<i>To your hunger-stricken eyes</i>

00:23:32.500 --> 00:23:40.375
<i>How does my body seem</i>

00:23:40.375 --> 00:23:48.250
<i>If you are to eat me, do it in one blow</i>

00:23:48.250 --> 00:23:57.042
<i>So that the meat does not get hard</i>

00:23:59.375 --> 00:24:00.625
People who know, know all about it,

00:24:00.625 --> 00:24:02.042
and those who don't know,
don't know. Well, of course.

00:24:02.042 --> 00:24:03.792
But there was a work that
was the prototype for Excel Saga,

00:24:03.792 --> 00:24:05.458
and it's called "Daitenzin".

00:24:05.458 --> 00:24:07.167
It seems that Mr. Rikdo's
<i>dojinshi </i>compilation of it

00:24:07.167 --> 00:24:09.750
is actually going at a pretty good
premium in used comic book stores

00:24:09.750 --> 00:24:11.583
in places like Nakano and
Ikebukuro. True story.

00:24:11.583 --> 00:24:13.417
The trio of idiots,
Watanabe, Iwata, and Sumiyoshi,

00:24:13.417 --> 00:24:14.542
do unbelievable things.

00:24:14.542 --> 00:24:16.208
And unbelievable things
are done to me, Excel.

00:24:16.208 --> 00:24:18.208
The plots are rather too
tempting for the good of children,

00:24:18.208 --> 00:24:20.417
but in any case, we'll throw away
our shame, reputation, and pride

00:24:20.417 --> 00:24:22.667
and next time, we'll try our hand
at "Municipal Force Daitenzin"!

00:24:22.667 --> 00:24:24.583
It's probably the first episode
in history based on a <i>dojinshi</i>.

00:24:24.583 --> 00:24:26.958
We're not afraid of criticism
from the anime critics and fans!

00:24:26.958 --> 00:24:28.594
We're not afraid!
